# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is deliberately tracked: this workspace ships applications
# (grafium, grafium-tui), so the lockfile is what makes a build reproducible.
# Leaving it untracked let a fresh checkout resolve a different llama-cpp-2
# patch release than the source expected and fail to compile.

# Node
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

